///- --package .
// BACKEND-COVERAGE-GAPS Zig Export arm regression (pack 5o). codegenZig had NO Export case (fell through to the
//     unsupported-op fallthrough); the fix mirrors codegenRust's export builder and lands via
//     apps/compiler/packs/apply-zig-export-pack.ps1. ///> zig ONLY: Export is a library entry, so a native-RUN
//     runner that links an exe fails on backends whose Export emits a library -- C has no Export arm at all (n54)
//     and Rust's Export emits a crate (rustc E0601 "no main"). Zig's Export emit keeps spiralMain, so the program
//     runs standalone and the zig target agrees (export_add(40,2)=42 -> exit 0; proven on the patched DLL, n56).
//     UNWIRED in package.spiproj; the 5o review runs it as a REQUIRED Cells gate (test-blocks.ps1 -Lib tests/families
//     -Files export_family.spi, memo off; zig must agree). Self-checking shape per SELF-CHECKING-SAMPLES.
:= export_add ((x, y) : i32 * i32) : i32 = x +. y

///> zig
test export_add_returns_zero =
    !!!!Export("spiral_add", export_add)
    := program () : i32 =
        := ~n = 40i32
        := got = ~~ export_add (n, 2i32)
        ? got =. 42i32 ?> 0i32 |: 1i32
    ? program () <> 0i32 ?> failwith "export_add"
